Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 22:50:34 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 3/7] NDNormalForm: the verifier's characterization, hV and its
 verdict on a display

Checkpoint 5 of the linear normal form's continuation: the verifier over the
work tapes from any entry (replay, return of tape 0, clear of tape 1, by
induction on the remaining tapes), the verifier's characterization from the
stream start (its first verdict, accepting exactly when every check passes,
with an empty output and a linear time bound then), the split of a stream that
first stops the controller into records, the backward lemma's obligation hV
in the host's terms, and the verifier's acceptance of a genuine display, whose
decoded virtual run is the genuine run.

